    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d1771">

                <pb facs="1157" n="1041" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg1041"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 819.74/37.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        Minister Price.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Extract.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-01-29">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">January 29, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Your despatch No. 69. Subject of agreement with Panama concerning the
                    establishment of radio telegraph stations in territory of that Republic has been
                    considered by the Joint Army and Navy Board. The report of that board was
                    approved by the President November 17, 1913.</p>
                <p>The first paragraph of this report provides for giving to United States
                    Government the monopoly of all means of radio communication <pb facs="1158"
                        n="1042" xml:id="pg1042"/> within the Panaman territory and cancelling of
                    all concessions for stations not at this time in actual operation, if such
                    exist.</p>
                <p>You are instructed to inform the Government of Panama in this sense in an
                    informal manner.</p>
                <p>Further instructions will be sent in near future.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
